total":0,"completed":0,"percent_completed":0},"issue_dependencies_summary":{"blocked_by":0,"total_blocked_by":0,"blocking":0,"total_blocking":0},"body":"### Tested versions\n\n4.6.1, 4.7 (from git)\n\n### System information\n\nGodot v4.7.dev (9095a76ff) - Windows 10 (build 19044) - Multi-window, 1 monitor - Direct3D 12 (Forward+) - dedicated Intel(R) Iris(R) Xe Graphics (Intel Corporation; 27.20.100.9664) - 11th Gen Intel(R) Core(TM) i7-1165G7 @ 2.80GHz (8 threads) - 39.84 GiB memory\n\n### Issue description\n\nCurrently, properties in the inspector, project settings, editor settings, etc., don't tell us what they actually do. As a (very obvious) example, I know that, e.g., `Node3D` has a `Position` property, but it doesn't tell me what that does. For `Position` the meaning is obvious, but for others this is not so.\n\nMy request is that the Accessible Description attribute be set on the property, if this information is available from code, describing what the property does. For example, if the property has a doc comment or the engine can figure out the documentation for this property, set this attribute to a (plane text) description of it. I'm not entirely sure how this works internally, so I hope this is enough detail. My idea is that, for something like inspector properties, the engine would just extract doc comments, and if a doc comment existed for that property, the engine would set the Accessible Description attribute for that property to the doc comment. This wouldn't be set on the inspector-generated controls for that property (e.g., x/y/z spin boxes for a Vector3), but on the property node itself.\n\n### Steps to reproduce\n\nUsing a screen reader (e.g., NVDA), open any project and go into the inspector or any of the settings dialogs. If you go to \"Property: X\" where `X` is the property name, what it does is uncertain.\n\n### Minimal reproduction project (MRP)\n\nN/A","closed_by":{"login":"Repiteo","id":17489292,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE3NDg5Mjky","avatar_u